{"parentUuid":"e803acb5-e0c3-4041-9bde-b99f7573c4e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt3MU7yrJeTXv9vsx1bj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Jobs and New request pages are committed as `dc15a41`, which is local and not pushed. Both CI runs from the last push passed, including the first iced build on Linux.\n\n**What's done in G2 so far:**\n- **Jobs:**\n  - All servers' jobs, the ones waiting on you first.\n  - The workspace filter and the search.\n  - A split job's parts listed under it.\n  - A note for each server that can't be read.\n  - \"New request\", and a click on a job that opens it on its own server.\n- **New request:**\n  - Server, workspace and workflow pickers.\n  - A multi-line request field, with Submit enabled only when it's ready.\n  - \"Start from a GitHub issue\".\n- A page reads again when a server push arrives.\n- The client's 14 tests pass, clippy is clean, and CodeScene passes.\n\n**What blocks a real test:** the stack is still stopped, so the server's store can't answer and the Jobs list stays empty. The page draws correctly and names `Two` as unreachable, but I can't check it against real jobs, or check the job page I'll build next, until the stack runs.\n\n**On your screen:** an \"Accessibility Access\" warning window is open. My earlier AppleScript attempt opened it, and you can dismiss it.\n\nMay I start the stack again so I can test the pages against real jobs? Meanwhile I'll keep going with the job page."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":497,"cache_read_input_tokens":477639,"output_tokens":573,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":125},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":497,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"in