{"parentUuid":"06904873-3661-46e1-b219-960de1f284f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt4mCipKNJKor2jd4TGU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HQk8jAxsVicVegb9ENtQiA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"so the window now shows `local` at once and adds the others when their tokens are read.\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\" Then Constraints (the charter's rules, the harness and factory ladders with history, promote and demote, and the form to add one), Capabilities (the charter's allows, the grants per stage, the factory's own), and the Audit Log (the chain's check, the writer's state, every entry, and Export), each seen live. Found live: the Keychain asks the person before a newly built `bastion-desktop` reads an added server's token, as its item trusts the Tauri app, so each rebuild asks again; and the Audit Log showed the audit writer failing with `database::query` not found since the stack stopped, and no entry for that stop, so a stop that takes the database down is not recorded (a server problem, left open).\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add PLAN.md && git commit -q -m \"G2: Constraints, Capabilities and the Audit Log in the native client\n\nA button that cannot be pressed now reads faded, and a rung keeps one\nwidth so the rules line up.\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Record and commit the governance pages"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":581255,"output_tokens":495,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":396,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_