{"parentUuid":"eee6a9a1-1060-427d-900a-7f40281ce545","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt4myMgCDiKvjoF7iaME","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Constraints, Capabilities and the Audit Log are done and committed as `a18ab81`. The stack is running again, and all three pages showed real data.\n\n**Two things need you:**\n1. **A Keychain prompt is open on your screen.** It asks whether `bastion-desktop` may read the token of the server `Two`. The Keychain item trusts the Tauri app, so the new client must ask. Each rebuild of the client during development asks again. Allow or deny it as you choose. Until you answer, `Two` stays out of the server list, and `local` works either way.\n2. **The audit lost a record.** The Audit Log page shows the audit writer failing with `database::query` not found since the stack stopped. The log also has no entry for that stop. A stop that takes the database down can lose its own audit record, which is why I couldn't tell who stopped the stack. This is a server problem, so I recorded it in the plan as an open item and didn't change the backend.\n\n**Fixed along the way:**\n- **Slow start:** a page waited about 7.5 s for the Keychain. The window now shows `local` at once and adds the other servers when their tokens arrive.\n- **Scroll:** a page kept the scroll of the page before it. Each page now starts at its top.\n- **Look:** buttons that can't be pressed now look faded, and the rung chips line up.\n\n**Checks:** the client has 23 tests, clippy is clean, and CodeScene passes.\n\n**Still to port in G2:** Evals, Engine, Settings, and Workflows (the canvas editor). I haven't pushed `f927270` or `a18ab81` yet. I'll push them with the next batch of pages unless you want them pushed now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":581651,"output_tokens":650,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":103},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":650,"cache_read_input_tokens":581651,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5ce5d53e-8dfa-492b-bd45-4e95ecb29a66","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgt4my1aUgDdHf1n4r8zi","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f9bd90b-d5b7-4a5a-9911-ee0dee0d0d1a","timestamp":"2026-11-09T21:29:48.877Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
