{"parentUuid":"15cbbb83-e4dd-45bf-ac49-f574601b0a14","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt5Bc9dv33kqD8NRBxpE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DLoUwVydCWAEBWVJ6KnMzt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"so a stop that takes the database down is not recorded (a server problem, left open).\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\" Then Engine: the link, the stack with Start and Stop, Doctor, the containers with stop, start and logs (each read waits for the lines after the last), functions and trigger types with a filter, and queues; seen live with 374 functions and every Doctor check passing, but the log view itself not yet seen. A push now says what changed (every job, one job, or the engine), so the Engine page reads again on an engine push and not on each job's; and a server back from down reads the page again, which the first version had backwards.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add PLAN.md && git commit -q -m \"G2: the Engine page and its console in the native client\n\nA push now says whether it changed every job, one job, or the engine, so\na page reads again only what it shows. A server back from down reads the\npage again; the first version had that backwards.\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Record and commit the Engine page"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":615553,"output_tokens":444,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":396,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":615553,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_creati